pump therapy in diabetes management.  \n  *Start Date:* June 2011\n\n---\n\n## Trials with Unknown or Withdrawn Status\n\n- **[NCT00628056](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00628056)**  \n  *Title:* Mechanisms Responsible for Cardiac and Skeletal Muscle Energetic Impairment in Diabetes  \n  *Focus:* Studied energetic impairments in diabetic cardiomyopathy.  \n  *Status:* Unknown  \n  *Start Date:* October 2006\n\n- **[NCT02683902](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02683902)**  \n  *Title:* The Effect of Hypocaloric Diet Associated With tDCS on Weight Loss and Metabolic Profile  \n  *Focus:* Assessed combined hypocaloric diet and transcranial direct current stimulation (tDCS) effects on weight loss and metabolism in prediabetes and obesity.  \n  *Status:* Unknown  \n  *Start Date:* March 2016\n\n- **[NCT00922402](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00922402)**  \n  *Title:* Heart & Diabetes - Feasibility Study  \n  *Focus:* Feasibility study on acute heart failure in diabetes patients.  \n  *Status:* Withdrawn  \n  *Start Date:* June 2009\n\n---\n\n## Ongoing and Recruiting Studies\n\n- **[NCT00026702](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00026702)**  \n  *Title:* Search for New Methods to Detect Acute Renal Failure  \n  *Focus:* Observational study aiming to identify novel detection methods for acute renal failure, relevant for diabetic kidney disease.  \n  *Status:* Recruiting  \n  *Start Date:* June 2000\n\n---\n\n## Practical Insights\n\n- **Emerging Therapies:** Phase 1 and 4 trials highlight ongoing development and evaluation of novel pharmacologic agents (e.g., LY3437943, SGLT-2 inhibitors) with potential benefits on glycemic control and cardiovascular/kidney outcomes in T2DM.\n- **Mechanistic Understanding:** Several studies focus on understanding metabolic pathways and the role of genetics, exercise, and receptor signaling in diabetes management, which may inform personalized treatment approaches.\n- **Technology in Diabetes Care:** Completed studies on 